{
  "title": "GC EMA outer band: years, cohorts and path scale",
  "summary": "Saved GC excursion means, coverage and horizon-specific evidence at a ten-bar cooldown. Annual regimes differ; MAE/MFE extrema and terminal rates do not establish executable profits.",
  "source": {
    "producer": "sahadeva",
    "runId": "20260925T223721Z_gc_ema_excursions_v1"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "question",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Question and selected scope",
      "body": "A completed five-minute GC close at or below EMA225 minus three population standard deviations of signed close-minus-EMA residuals is followed from the next complete unadjusted open. The annual view fixes cooldown at ten following bars and horizon at twenty five-minute bars (100 minutes). The 2026 horizon view retains the saved seven horizons; it does not pool their outcomes."
    },
    {
      "id": "findings",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Supported findings",
      "body": "The saved yearly table reports both adverse and favorable path extrema rather than choosing an MFE exit. Coverage, valid denominators and uncertainty differ by year. The larger cooldown/horizon grid is a correlated sensitivity, not independent replication or optimized trading evidence."
    },
    {
      "kind": "figure",
      "id": "yearly-figure",
      "title": "Annual path scale at the saved default",
      "path": "figures/yearly-excursions.png",
      "alt": "Separate adverse and favorable annual GC excursion means with saved interval endpoints; both increase markedly in 2025 and 2026.",
      "caption": "Exact yearly.csv values at cooldown 10 and horizon 20. Dots are means; vertical lines are approximate 95% normal ISO-week cluster intervals, unadjusted for multiple comparisons. GC points; 2010 partial and 2026 YTD. Extrema have unknown ordering and are not executable exits.",
      "referenceIds": [
        "yearly-source"
      ]
    },
