      "id": "methods",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Definitions and methods",
      "body": "Cooldown C suppresses the C following bars after an accepted signal; suppressed candidates do not restart it. The next contiguous full five-minute bar supplies the unadjusted entry reference. Every measured future bar must be complete and keep one contract and adjustment. MAE is adverse excursion, MFE favorable excursion, and terminal movement is the final close minus entry. Saved mean bounds use approximate 95% normal ISO-week cluster intervals; no interval for terminal-positive rate is manufactured."
    },
    {
      "id": "limitations",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Limitations and uncertainty",
      "body": "Coverage begins partway through 2010 and 2026 is YTD through September 18. Whole-day and adjusted continuous history eligibility is retrospective rather than point-in-time. Missing minutes, partial bars, gaps and roll/adjustment changes exclude paths. No stops, fees, fills, slippage or net profitability were tested; the saved interactive report is not imported into the public page."
    },
